{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/3/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内\"种子\"像素的颜色，在区域边框的图例映射表中查找对应的填充图案方向，然后用种子颜色沿该方向绘制平行条纹填满整个封闭区域。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干由 grey 像素围成的封闭矩形区域（一像素宽的边框）。\n  - 每个封闭区域内部恰好有一个孤立的\"种子\"像素，颜色各不相同（如 red、blue、green 等）。\n  - 网格的一条边缘处有一个图例区域：图例由若干小矩形格子组成，每个格子左半部分填一种颜色，右半部分绘有该颜色对应的条纹方向示意——水平条纹（同色像素排成一行）或垂直条纹（同色像素排成一列）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 识别每个 grey 边框封闭区域内部的种子像素颜色 C。\n  - 在边缘图例中查找颜色 C 对应的条纹方向（水平或垂直）。\n  - 将该封闭区域内部所有背景像素用颜色 C 按照图例指定的方向绘制间隔条纹：若为水平方向，则从区域内部顶行开始，奇数行填充颜色 C、偶数行保持背景色；若为垂直方向，则从区域内部最左列开始，奇数列填充颜色 C、偶数列保持背景色。种子像素本身被条纹覆盖（视为区域内普通像素）。\n  - Grey 边框和图例区域保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现边缘图例是一张\"颜色→条纹方向\"的映射表，再将每个区域内种子的颜色与图例匹配以确定填充方式——仅靠种子颜色或仅靠区域形状都无法推断出正确的输出。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中散落的同色碎片按颜色分组拼合成完整矩形，拼合后矩形的放置位置由同色\"锚点\"标记决定，锚点成为拼合矩形的指定角。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 每种前景色恰好出现两类对象：(1) 若干分散的小型 4-连通碎片，它们的像素总面积恰好能拼成一个整数边长的实心矩形；(2) 一个孤立的单像素\"锚点\"。\n  - 不同颜色的碎片和锚点互不重叠、互不相邻。\n  - 每种颜色的锚点位于其所有碎片的包围盒的某个角方向的外侧（左上、右上、左下、右下之一）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种前景色，统计该颜色所有碎片的总像素数 N，将 N 分解为最接近正方形的矩形尺寸（即选择使长宽之差最小的因子对 a×b，a≤b）。\n  - 找到该颜色的锚点像素位置，判断锚点相对于碎片群包围盒中心的方位（左上、右上、左下、右下）。\n  - 以锚点为对应角，绘制 a×b 的实心矩形（例如锚点在左上方位则锚点为矩形左上角）。\n  - 清除该颜色原有的所有碎片像素。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成两步非平凡推理：第一步是发现碎片总面积决定矩形尺寸（需要数像素并找到最接近正方形的因子分解）；第二步是发现孤立锚点的方位角决定矩形的对齐角——两层信息缺一不可。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格中找到被\"遮罩色\"部分覆盖的隐藏形状，利用网格边缘的\"形状字典\"识别每个隐藏形状的完整轮廓，然后用该形状字典中对应的输出颜色替换遮罩区域，还原完整形状。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格主体区域包含若干前景色形状，其中一些形状被 grey 像素部分遮盖——grey 像素覆盖了形状的某些位置，使形状看起来不完整。\n  - 网格的顶部或底部边缘有一排\"形状字典\"：每个字典条目是一个小矩形框，内部绘有一个完整的小型模板形状（用某种颜色绘制），旁边紧挨一个单像素的\"输出色标\"。\n  - 主体区域中每个被遮盖的形状，其可见部分（非 grey 像素）与字典中某个模板形状的子集匹配，且颜色相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 在形状字典中读取每个模板形状及其对应的输出色标颜色。\n  - 对主体区域中每个含有 grey 遮盖像素的前景形状，将其可见像素与字典模板逐一比对，找到唯一匹配的模板。\n  - 根据匹配模板的完整轮廓，将该形状中被 grey 覆盖的位置还原为模板形状的像素，但还原的像素使用字典中对应的输出色标颜色（而非原始形状颜色）。\n  - 形状的原始可见像素保持原色不变；字典区域在输出中移除（替换为背景色）。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题需要三层推理——首先识别边缘字典的结构（模板+色标配对），然后通过部分可见像素与模板的形状匹配来确定被遮盖的完整形状，最后用色标颜色（而非原色）填回遮盖区域，这三步环环相扣。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个前景对象沿其内部\"箭头标记\"所指方向平移，平移距离等于同色边框围栏内的空心孔洞数量。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干不同颜色的前景对象，每个对象由两部分组成：(1) 一个主体形状（任意 4-连通形状，面积 ≥ 3 像素）；(2) 主体形状内部嵌有一个由三个同色像素组成的 L 形\"箭头标记\"，箭头标记与主体同色，其 L 形的朝向指示一个基本方向（上、下、左、右——L 形的长边指向的方向即为移动方向）。\n  - 网格中另有若干与前景对象同色的单像素宽矩形边框\"围栏\"（边框内部为背景色或包含背景色的孔洞）。每种颜色恰好有一个围栏与之对应。\n  - 围栏内部可能有 0 到若干个由背景色构成的独立孔洞（4-连通背景色区域，被围栏边框完全包围）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种前景色，找到该颜色的主体对象和围栏。\n  - 读取主体对象内部 L 形箭头标记的朝向，确定平移方向。\n  - 数围栏内部的背景色孔洞数量 K。\n  - 将主体对象（含箭头标记）沿箭头方向平移 K 个像素。原始位置清为背景色。\n  - 围栏保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要同时破解两个独立编码：对象内部的 L 形标记编码了移动方向，而同色围栏中的孔洞数量编码了移动距离——方向和距离来自完全不同的视觉线索源，必须分别识别并关联到同一颜色才能得出正确变换。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每个\"信号源\"像素发出的射线在遇到镜面时反射，射线最终命中的目标格被染上信号源的颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干 azure 色的单像素宽 45 度对角线段，充当\"镜面\"（每段长度 ≥ 2 像素，方向为左上-右下或左下-右上）。\n  - 网格边缘上有若干不同颜色的孤立\"信号源\"像素（非 azure、非背景色），每个信号源位于网格的上、下、左、右某一条边上。\n  - 网格内部散布若干 grey 色的\"目标格\"像素。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 每个信号源从其位置向网格内部发射一条垂直于所在边的直线射线（上边缘的向下，左边缘的向右，依此类推）。\n  - 射线沿直线前进，遇到 azure 镜面时发生 90 度反射：遇到左上-右下方向（\\）的镜面，水平射线变为垂直、垂直射线变为水平（类似光线反射）；遇到左下-右上方向（/）的镜面同理反射。\n  - 射线持续前进直到命中一个 grey 目标格或到达网格边界（若到达边界则该射线无效果）。\n  - 若射线命中 grey 目标格，将该目标格重新着色为射线信号源的颜色。\n  - 镜面、信号源、以及未被命中的目标格保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者必须先理解 azure 对角线段是镜面而非障碍物，然后在心理上模拟每条射线的反射路径——关键难点在于发现射线不是被镜面阻挡而是被反射转向，这与直觉中\"碰到东西就停下\"的模式完全不同。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在由隔板分割的多个子区域中，每个子区域内的彩色像素\"投票\"决定该区域的统一填充色，但投票规则由隔板颜色隐含编码：一种隔板色表示\"多数色获胜\"，另一种隔板色表示\"少数色获胜\"。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格被两种不同颜色的单像素宽直线隔板分割成若干矩形子区域。隔板颜色仅有两种（如 grey 和 maroon），每条隔板完整贯穿网格的一行或一列。\n  - 每个子区域内部散布着若干彩色像素（非背景、非隔板色），每个区域内恰好有两种不同的前景色，数量可能不等。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 确定包围每个子区域的隔板颜色。若区域四边的隔板（或网格边界）中，隔板颜色以某一种为主（出现次数更多的隔板色），则以该主隔板色决定投票规则。\n  - 若主隔板色为 grey：该区域采用\"多数规则\"——区域内像素数较多的前景色获胜，整个区域内部全部填充为该色。\n  - 若主隔板色为 maroon：该区域采用\"少数规则\"——区域内像素数较少的前景色获胜，整个区域内部全部填充为该色。\n  - 若两种前景色数量相等，则保留靠近区域左上角的那种颜色。\n  - 隔板像素保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要发现区域内多色像素是一种\"投票\"，然后需要发现不同颜色的隔板编码了相反的投票规则（多数 vs 少数）——第二层发现是关键的隐蔽机制，仅观察单个区域无法区分两种规则，必须跨区域对比才能归纳出隔板颜色与投票逻辑的关联。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每对同色标记像素用直线连接，连线在交叉点处按照\"先水平后垂直\"的绘制优先级叠加颜色，交叉点最终显示垂直线段的颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干种前景色，每种颜色恰好出现两个孤立像素作为\"端点标记\"。\n  - 每对同色端点要么共享同一行、要么共享同一列、要么既不同行也不同列。\n  - 端点之间不存在其他前景像素。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每对同色端点，用该颜色绘制连接它们的曼哈顿 L 形路径：先从一个端点水平画到与另一个端点同列的位置，再垂直画到另一个端点。若两端点同行则直接画水平线，同列则直接画垂直线。\n  - 当多条路径经过同一像素时，该像素的颜色由最后绘制的垂直线段决定（垂直段覆盖水平段）。\n  - 绘制顺序：各颜色之间的绘制不影响最终结果，因为覆盖规则始终是\"垂直段优先于水平段\"——任何像素若同时被某条路径的水平段和另一条路径的垂直段经过，显示垂直段的颜色。\n  - 端点像素保持其原色不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现每对同色点通过 L 形折线连接（而非直线），然后发现交叉点的颜色不是简单叠加或先后覆盖，而是由\"垂直段始终优先于水平段\"这一隐含规则决定——必须通过观察多个交叉点的颜色来归纳出这条方向性优先规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中的每个彩色对象根据其所在象限被施加不同的变换（旋转 0°/90°/180°/270°），象限与旋转角度的对应关系由网格中心的\"罗盘\"图案编码。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格尺寸为奇数×奇数，中心有一个 3×3 的\"罗盘\"图案：罗盘的中心像素为 grey，上下左右四个相邻像素各为不同颜色（从 red、blue、green、yellow 中选四种），四个对角像素为背景色。\n  - 网格以中心行和中心列为界分成四个象限（不含中心行列本身）。\n  - 每个象限内有恰好一个由某种非背景、非罗盘色的前景色构成的小型 4-连通对象（面积 ≤ 6 像素）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 读取罗盘图案：中心像素上方的颜色对应\"上\"方向，右方对应\"右\"，下方对应\"下\"，左方对应\"左\"。\n  - 建立象限到旋转角度的映射：罗盘上方颜色指示\"不旋转\"（0°），罗盘右方颜色指示\"顺时针 90°\"，罗盘下方颜色指示\"180°\"，罗盘左方颜色指示\"逆时针 90°\"（即顺时针 270°）。但这些颜色不直接对应象限——而是每个象限边界上（中心行或中心列上）与该象限相邻的两个罗盘臂颜色中，位于顺时针方向较后的那个颜色决定该象限的旋转。\n  - 具体地：右上象限由罗盘\"右\"臂颜色决定旋转角度；右下象限由罗盘\"下\"臂颜色决定；左下象限由罗盘\"左\"臂颜色决定；左上象限由罗盘\"上\"臂颜色决定。\n  - 对每个象限内的对象，以其自身中心为旋转中心，施加对应角度的旋转，结果留在原象限内。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先要识别中心 3×3 图案是一个方向编码罗盘，然后要建立罗盘臂颜色→旋转角度→象限的三重映射关系——关键难点在于罗盘臂与象限的对应规则本身需要从样例中归纳，不能仅靠空间直觉猜出。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/3/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a2d730bd\" lines=\"43-56\">\n<description>\nExtend each solid foreground rectangle toward its same-color isolated pixels with capped one-cell paths, clearing each original marker pixel.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each foreground color has exactly one solid rectangular object and one or more isolated same-color marker pixels.\n- Every marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the rectangle bbox and lies outside it.\nRule\n- For each marker, draw a one-cell-wide straight path from the adjacent side of the rectangle through one cell beyond the marker.\n- Add a three-pixel perpendicular cap at the rectangle end and around the marker endpoint.\n- Recolor the original marker pixel to background.\nKey insight\n- The isolated pixels are not copied; they mark the hollow endpoints of capped protrusions grown from their matching rectangle.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5623160b\" lines=\"44-59\">\n<description>\nPush every colored object touching maroon markers straight outward until it reaches the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Maroon pixels are fixed markers.\n- Every other foreground 4-connected object touches the marker pixels on exactly one cardinal side.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each non-background, non-maroon object from its original position.\n- Translate it in the direction away from its maroon contact until the object reaches the grid boundary.\n- Keep the maroon marker pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The maroon contact side is a launcher: it determines a unique outward ray for the whole object, and the edge of the grid determines the translation distance.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e84fef15\" lines=\"39-59\">\n<description>\nReconstruct the repeated tile from its separated copies and mark the missing pixels in the damaged copy blue.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a lattice of equal-size blocks separated by one-cell solid rows\n  and columns of the same separator color.\n- All blocks are copies of one motif except exactly one block, where some\n  motif pixels have been overwritten by the motif background color.\n- Blue is absent from the input and is reserved as the output marker color.\n\nRule:\n- Recover the motif by taking the unique majority color at each local block\n  coordinate across all block copies.\n- Find the single block that differs from this consensus motif.\n- Return the consensus motif, recoloring the differing local coordinates blue.\n\nKey insight:\n- The repeated copies provide redundancy: the damaged positions are exactly\n  the coordinates where the lone nonconforming copy has background instead of\n  the consensus motif color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8fff9e47\" lines=\"8-25\">\n<description>\nTurn a 4-cell-wide strip of 2x2 blocks into four nested corner-fill patterns.\n\nInput structure\nThe input is an even-sized rectangle whose shorter dimension is four pixels.\nIt can be partitioned exactly into 2x2 blocks, giving one block for each layer\nof the output quadrants.\n\nRule\nRead the 2x2 blocks in reverse row-major order: bottom-right block first,\nmoving left, then moving upward. For each block, send its top-left,\ntop-right, bottom-left, and bottom-right pixels to the layer sequences of the\nupper-left, upper-right, lower-left, and lower-right output quadrants.\n\nKey insight\nEach input 2x2 block supplies the four colors for one concentric layer, and\nthe layer order is the block order from bottom-right back to top-left.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f5f939b\" lines=\"42-57\">\n<description>\nMark the missing center of each plus-shaped arrangement of four two-pixel bars with yellow.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The single foreground color forms isolated 4-connected objects, each a horizontal or vertical two-pixel bar.\n- Some bars form an implied plus sign: two horizontal bars and two vertical bars around an empty center, with a one-pixel gap between the center and each bar.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input unchanged except at implied plus-sign centers.\n- For every background pixel with foreground bars at offsets 2-3 cells left, right, above, and below, recolor that center yellow.\n- The one-pixel gaps immediately next to the center in the four cardinal directions must remain background.\n\nKey insight:\n- The yellow pixels are not extending a line; they identify the shared missing center where four separated two-pixel bars align as a plus sign.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1478ab18\" lines=\"35-43\">\n<description>\nPaint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is an orange background with exactly four foreground marker pixels of one color. The markers have a square bounding box: three markers are bbox corners, and the fourth marker is inside that square.\nRule\nFind the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.\nKey insight\nThe present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"71e489b6\" lines=\"7-19\">\n<description>\nHighlight black defects in blue foreground by surrounding them with orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- Blue (1) foreground on black (0) bg; small black holes or protrusions within blue regions; occasional thin blue spurs into black areas.\n\nRule:\n- Thin blue pixels mostly surrounded by black are absorbed into the background.\n- Small black components (≤3 cells) and leaf pixels of larger black components are \"defects.\"\n- Each defect gets an orange (7) 8-neighbor halo; the defect pixels themselves stay black.\n\nKey insight: Only structural anomalies—tiny isolated patches and dangling endpoints—are marked, not bulk black regions.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f3e14006\" lines=\"21-39\">\n<description>\nBuild the woven rectangle determined by the two marked cells on each crossed bar.\n\nInput structure\nA black-background grid contains one long horizontal bar and one long vertical bar.\nEach bar has a dominant base color and exactly two same-colored marker pixels.\n\nRule\nThe horizontal marker pair gives the output column span.  From the horizontal bar\nrow, walk toward the farther vertical marker; rows and columns alternate every\nother cell.  Even step/even offset cells use the horizontal marker color until\nthe nearer vertical marker is reached, then use the vertical marker color.\nOdd row steps use the horizontal base on marker columns and the original\ncrossing color on spacer columns.  Spacer columns on even row steps use the\nvertical base, except at the switch row where they use the crossing color.\n\nKey insight\nThe original cross cell records which base color wins at base/base lattice\ncrossings; the nearer vertical marker is the color-switch boundary.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"37ce87bb\" lines=\"33-47\">\n<description>\nCompute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.\n- The penultimate column is an empty result slot.\n\nRule\n- Keep every input bar unchanged.\n- Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.\n- Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.\n\nKey insight\n- The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8e301a54\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nMove every foreground object straight downward by a number of rows equal to its own pixel count.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\n- The foreground is made of separated 4-connected monochromatic objects.\n- Objects may move partly below the bottom edge of the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the canvas to the background.\n- For each foreground object, compute its area in pixels.\n- Redraw the object at the same columns and that many rows lower, clipping pixels below the grid.\n\nKey insight:\n- The downward displacement is the object's own area; color and shape only identify which pixels move together.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"11dc524f\" lines=\"25-40\">\n<description>\nSlide the non-square sprite to the square anchor and replace the anchor with the sprite's mirror image.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- There is one 8-connected non-background sprite that is not a solid 2x2 square.\n- There is one solid 2x2 square anchor in another non-background color.\n\nRule:\n- Move the sprite straight toward the anchor along their unique cardinal separation until it touches the anchor's near edge.\n- Reflect the moved sprite across that near edge and draw the reflected copy in the anchor color.\n- Clear the original locations; the output keeps only the moved sprite and reflected anchor-color copy.\n\nKey insight:\n- The 2x2 square marks the mirror line: its side facing the sprite becomes the contact edge for a two-color reflected pair.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"52df9849\" lines=\"49-67\">\n<description>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
